<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martanda Bhairava Thondaiman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1875">1875</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martanda Bhairava Thondaiman was Raja of Pudukkottai, a princely state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, from 1886 to 1928. He spent much of his reign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, and his marriage to the Australian Molly Fink in 1915 caused friction with the British authorities. He renounced the throne in 1928 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> that year.</p></div>
